# NO TRAILING SLASHES on directory entries in this file (#455).
#
# A trailing slash matches DIRECTORIES ONLY. Any of these paths can legitimately
# be a SYMLINK instead — a worktree reaching a shared cache, a shared dependency
# install — and the slashed form leaves a symlink untracked-but-NOT-ignored. A
# committed symlink stores its TARGET STRING as blob content, i.e. an absolute
# path off this machine, in a public repo.
#
# `.github/scripts/check-no-home-paths.sh` cannot catch that: it greps the
# working-tree PATH, and grep follows the symlink into the target directory, so
# it matches nothing while the blob itself holds the leaking string. This file is
# the only defence against that specific leak, so it fails toward over-ignoring.
#
# Verified before this was applied: zero TRACKED paths match any of these names,
# so dropping the slashes cannot shadow anything in the repo.

# Dependencies
node_modules
app/node_modules
pipeline/node_modules

# Build outputs
dist
app/dist
*.tsbuildinfo

# Test artifacts
coverage
playwright-report
app/playwright-report
test-results
app/test-results

# Pipeline intermediate downloads (raw source data, not the packed outputs)
pipeline/raw
pipeline/data-src
pipeline/.venv
pipeline/bin

# Local/session files
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/worktrees
.superpowers
.remember
graphify-out
.playwright-mcp
.env
.env.*

# Docs-only wind fixtures (#459/#462): the generator is committed
# (app/scripts/gen-docs-wind-fixture.mjs) and regenerating is already a
# mandatory pre-recapture step (its forecast horizon drifts in ~6 days), so
# the generated output would be dead weight in git history and in every
# deployed ref (app/public/** is copied verbatim into dist) for bytes nobody
# is ever meant to read against directly. Exact filename, not a glob over
# test-fixtures/, so this can never shadow the E2E suite's committed
# wind-sw12.json or any future e2e fixture added under the same directory.
app/public/test-fixtures/wind-docs-plan-route.json

# OS noise
.DS_Store
